<head><component name='Rendering' level='5'/><component name='Shape' level='4'/><component name='Lighting' level='3'/><component name='Interpolation' level='5'/><component name='EventUtilities' level='1'/><component name='Networking' level='3'/><meta name='title' content='giza-nest.x3d'/><meta name='description' content='Giza v2.1 (plateau, Sphinx, temples, Osiris Shaft) nested in the Gobbler, with a disco layer and a hypothetical Hall of Records. Synthetic and schematic: a simulacrum, not a survey.'/><meta name='hall-of-records' content="Hypothetical. Edgar Cayce (1930s readings) placed a &quot;Hall of Records&quot; under the Sphinx; a 1991 seismic survey reported a cavity under the left paw that was never excavated. The chamber drawn here is invented: its size, depth and contents are guesses for the picture, not data."/></head>
<Scene>
<WorldInfo title='Giza, disco night (nested in the Gobbler)' info='"Giza v2.1 files, unchanged except the Khufu level of detail forced to its mesh" "the disco layer and the Hall of Records are additions; the Hall is hypothetical"'/>
